    "done_when": "per §9's prototype: write 18 natural-language queries about JT-60SA, 12 answered by ingested code and 6 by ingested wiki or document content, each with one sentence naming what a correct answer contains, and store them in /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/imas-codex/search-rerank-prototype/queries.json; for each, call _search_code or _search_docs from imas_codex/llm/search_tools.py with facility jt-60sa for the top 30 candidates and label each candidate relevant or not against that sentence, recording the labels and the candidate text you judged in labels.json beside it; rerank each query's 30 candidates by one Jev Score per candidate (POST https://openrouter.ai/api/alpha/decisions, model typesafe/jev-1.13, key from get_api_key_for_service('facility-discovery'), state {query, candidate: {path or title, first 1500 characters of its text}}, question type score with five concrete levels from 'unrelated to the query' to 'directly answers the query'); compute nDCG@10 and mean reciprocal rank for the embedding order and the reranked order, per query and averaged, plus the rerank's cost and p50 and p95 latency per query; keep the scripts beside the data; write the evidence fragment with the two orders' metrics, a per-query table, and one figure of per-query nDCG@10 for both orders (data-ink style, SVG); no repository code change, no graph write and no discover run",
